3. Entity — Employee.java (with sensitive field)
The entity keeps the full, persistent shape of the record, including password, which must never be serialized
directly into an API response.
src/main/java/com/example/employeeapi/entity/Employee.java
package com.example.employeeapi.entity;
import jakarta.persistence.*;
import lombok.AllArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Data;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;
@Entity
@Table(name = "employees")
@Data
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class Employee {
 @Id
 @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
 private int empId;
 private String empName;
 private String department;
 private Double salary;
 // Sensitive field - persisted, but NEVER exposed via the REST API.
 private String password;
}
4. DTO — EmployeeDTO.java (safe subset)
The DTO is the API contract: it deliberately excludes salary and password, so no matter what the
controller does, those fields can never be serialized to the client.
src/main/java/com/example/employeeapi/dto/EmployeeDTO.java
package com.example.employeeapi.dto;
import lombok.AllArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Data;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;
/**
 * The shape of an Employee as seen by API clients.
 * Only fields safe to expose - no salary, no password.
 */
@Data
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class EmployeeDTO {
 private int empId;
 private String empName;
 private String department;
}
5. Mapper — EmployeeMapper.java
src/main/java/com/example/employeeapi/mapper/EmployeeMapper.java
package com.example.employeeapi.mapper;
import com.example.employeeapi.dto.EmployeeDTO;
import com.example.employeeapi.entity.Employee;
/**
 * Static utility for converting between the persistent Employee entity
 * and the EmployeeDTO exposed by the REST API.
 */
public class EmployeeMapper {
 private EmployeeMapper() {
 // utility class - no instances
 }
 // Entity -> DTO : used whenever data leaves the server
 public static EmployeeDTO toDto(Employee e) {
 if (e == null) {
 return null;
 }
 EmployeeDTO dto = new EmployeeDTO();
 dto.setEmpId(e.getEmpId());
 dto.setEmpName(e.getEmpName());
 dto.setDepartment(e.getDepartment());
 // salary and password are intentionally NOT copied
 return dto;
 }
 // DTO -> Entity : used when creating a brand-new Employee.
 // salary/password are left null - they are never supplied by clients.
 public static Employee toEntity(EmployeeDTO d) {
 if (d == null) {
 return null;
 }
 Employee employee = new Employee();
 employee.setEmpId(d.getEmpId());
 employee.setEmpName(d.getEmpName());
 employee.setDepartment(d.getDepartment());
 return employee;
 }
}
