9. Why the DTO Pattern Matters Here
• Entity — the full persistent shape (empId, empName, department, salary, password), used only
inside the server.
• DTO — the API contract (empId, empName, department), the only shape a client ever sees.
• Mapper — the single, centralized place where the conversion happens, so no controller method can
accidentally return an Employee (and leak password) by forgetting to map it.
• Because the controller's return types are EmployeeDTO/List<EmployeeDTO> everywhere, Jackson has
no password field to serialize in the first place — the leak is prevented structurally, not by an annotation like
@JsonIgnore that could be missed.
